// pf_site.vfl - PRIM wrangle.  B0's WRITE side: §12.4's site contract, stamped.
//
// Reads only the `_*` scratch `pf_site_in.vfl` captured off the INPUT; writes
// only the contract.  Splitting the two is what makes the tests in that file
// honest - see its header.
//
// ⛔ EVERY WRITE BELOW IS UNCONDITIONAL, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE POINT OF THIS
// FILE.  §12.4's `pf_setback` sentinel reads `>= 0` authored, negative absent -
// and a Houdini float attribute has NO absent value: every vertex carries one
// the moment the attribute exists.  So a B0 that merely CREATES `pf_setback`
// and writes only the edges it authors leaves every other edge at the created
// default of 0.0, and 0.0 now MEANS "build to the lot line".
//
// ⚠️ The lot below is named by its SIZE and not by its style, because
// `no_style_branching` forbids a style id anywhere in production source and it
// caught this very comment naming one.  It is the 10 x 90 farmstead lot.
//
// `R4-2` measured that exact B0 on that lot: plan box
// [0, 0, 10, 90] where the template asks [2.5, 2.0, 7.5, 47.0] - the building
// hard on its lot line - with **all four `pf_warn_*` at 0**, and `pf_setback`
// swept from the output by `CLEAN`, so the shipped geometry carries no trace
// of the request.  Silent, unwarned and untraceable.  The loop below therefore
// has NO branch that can leave an edge unwritten: -1.0 is what an edge gets
// when nothing authored it, and it is written, not defaulted.
//
// ⛔ WHAT THIS CANNOT DO, AND THE FIRST BUILD PUT THE BOUNDARY IN THE WRONG
// PLACE.  It said the omission was closed "for every stream that passes
// THROUGH B0" and that the residual was a stream that SKIPS B0.  Measured by
// an independent audit: a lot arriving with a HAND-CREATED vertex
// `pf_setback` - one edge authored 5.0 and the rest left at the 0.0 a fresh
// float attribute gives them - passes straight THROUGH this node and comes out
// [5.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], and the building lands at plan box
// [0.0, 5.0, 30.0, 24.0]: hard on the lot line on three of its four edges,
// with all four `pf_warn_*` at 0 and `pf_setback` swept from the output by
// `CLEAN`.  Controls: no attribute -> [2.5, 3.0, 28.0, 20.0]; the sentinel
// authored by hand -> [2.5, 5.0, 28.0, 20.0].
// ⛔ SO THE GUARANTEE IS "EVERY STREAM WHOSE LOT CARRIES NO VERTEX
// `pf_setback`", NOT "every stream through B0" - and hand-authoring is exactly
// the cascade level-5 workflow the attribute exists for.  ⚠️ B0 is not on the
// critical path either: the same hand-authored lot fed straight into
// `build()`, skipping B0 altogether, gives the identical lot-line building,
// and a lot with no `pf_setback` at all builds correctly without B0.  This
// node supplies defaults; nothing downstream asks whether it ran.
// The cure is a companion mask (`pf_setback_set`), which is a schema change
// and is Hannes' (§0.0g row 9); it is recommended there and deliberately not
// taken here.

int pts[] = primpoints(0, @primnum);

setprimattrib(0, "pf_site_id", @primnum, i@_site);
setprimattrib(0, "pf_seed", @primnum, i@_seed);
setprimattrib(0, "pf_style_template", @primnum, s@_style);

// ⚠️ Typed locals, not the ternary or the bare call: `vertex()` returns an
// untyped value and `setvertexattrib()` is overloaded on the last argument
// (dev-loop trap list).
for (int k = 0; k < len(pts); k++) {
    int vi = vertexindex(0, @primnum, k);
    float sb = vertex(0, "_setback", vi);
    string rl = vertex(0, "_role", vi);
    setvertexattrib(0, "pf_setback", @primnum, k, sb);
    setvertexattrib(0, "pf_face_role", @primnum, k, rl);
}
